The walk also covers the rest of `ooda/std`. Scanned count: 4754.

## 4. Cluster rollup

Cluster paths use substring matches (`/crypto`, `/net`, `/simd`, `/embedded_hal`, `/ai_ml`, `/deep_ai`, `/formal_verif`).
Crypto includes `crypto_advanced` and related trees. Network includes `net_telemetry`. Hardware is SIMD plus `embedded_hal`.

| Cluster | Files | Call-vs-token violations |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Crypto | 222 | 0 |
| FS | 12 | 0 |
| Network | 91 | 0 |
| Hardware | 58 | 0 |
| AI/ML | 51 | 0 |
| Formal Verification | 52 | 0 |

Total violations on the full std walk: 0.
Isolation verdict: CLEAN.

An earlier unanchored `str_contains` scan reported 26 hits. Those were identifier fragments and English words, not sealed calls.

## 5. What a violation means

The file contains a sealed call `op(` and does not name a matching `&Cap` token.
Do not treat this matrix as a compiler proof.
Do not treat it as SHIPPED emit+gcc GREEN.

Fix path for a true ambient call: pass the token in the function signature and down to the sealed op.

## 6. Zero Ambient Authority

On this call-anchored text audit, 4754 std modules have no unmatched sealed call of the listed ops.
Re-run: from `openOODA/`, `../ooda/bin/ooda run ./scripts/audit_library_capabilities.oo`.

Also see:
  - `openOODA/SECURITY.oot` — op matrix
